 "text": "..title\nAn ordinance approving a greenway participation agreement between the Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County, acting by and through the Board of Parks and Recreation and Department of Water and Sewerage Services, and Jeff Zeitlin for the construction of certain greenway improvements. (Proposal No. 2026M-056AG-001)\n..body\nWHEREAS, the Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County (“Metro”), by and through the Board of Parks and Recreation, maintains certain property as part of the Metro greenway system; and,\nWHEREAS, a portion of the greenway has been constructed upon property owned by Metro, by and through the Department of Water and Sewerage Services, consisting of approximately 2.6 acres of property located at 1508 3rd Avenue North (Map/Parcel No. 08205012700); and,\nWHEREAS, the parties have negotiated the terms of a participation agreement that will authorize Jeff Zeitlin to construct improvements within a portion of the Greenway and will be responsible for the ongoing care and maintenance of the improvements; and, \nWHEREAS, approval of the participation agreement will benefit the citizens of Nashville and Davidson County. \nNOW, THEREFORE, BE IT ENACTED BY THE COUNCIL OF THE METROPOLITAN GOVERNMENT OF NASHVILLE AND DAVIDSON COUNTY:\nSection 1.\tThat the participation agreement between the Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County, acting by and through the Board of Parks and Recreation and the Department of Water and Sewerage Services, and Jeff Zeitlin for the construction of greenway improvements attached hereto and incorporated herein, is hereby approved. \nSection 2. \tAmendments to this ordinance may be approved by resolution.\nSection 3. \tThis ordinance shall take effect from and after its final passage, the welfare of the Metropolitan Government of Nashville and Davidson County requiring it.\n..Agenda Analysis\nAnalysis\n\nThis ordinance approves a greenway participation agreement between the Metropolitan Board of Parks and Recreation (“Metro Parks”) and Department of Water and Sewerage Services, and Jeff Zeitlin for the construction of certain greenway improvements.\n\nA portion of the greenway has been constructed upon 2.6 acres of property owned by the Metropolitan Department of Water and Sewerage Services at 1508 3rd Avenue North. \n\nThe participation agreement authorizes Jeff Zeitlin to construct improvements within a portion of the greenway and be responsible for the ongoing care and maintenance of the improvements. Mr. Zeitlin owns adjacent property and intends to construct greenway improvements on the adjacent property as well. Those improvements are shown in an attachment to the agreement.\n\nThe participation agreement requires that the greenway be open and accessible for use throughout the duration of the project. The agreement is contingent on Mr. Zeitlin obtaining final site plan approval from Metro Parks’ Greenway Division and a final specific plan approval from all Metropolitan agencies. Mr. Zeitlin would be responsible for all costs of the improvements and furnish and maintain commercial general liability insurance naming the Metropolitan Government as an additional insured party in an amount no less than $1,000,000. Mr. Zeitlin would indemnify and hold harmless the Metropolitan Government from all claims from negligent or intentional acts of omissions of Mr. Zeitlin, as well as any claims tied to a failure to observe applicable laws.\n\nThis ordinance has been approved by the Planning Commission. Future amendments to this ordinance may be approved by resolution.\n\nFiscal Note: There is no cost to Metro for the performance of this agreement.\n\n"
}
